nes, which many could carry an aircraft, and the Sentaka I-200-Class that reached the highest submerged speed of WWII. Despite having an advanced submarine fleet they were built in relatively small numbers and they were less effective than German submarines. The reason was the Japanese naval doctrine which focused on large and decisive fleet battles, and consequently the submarines were used against warships rather than merchant ships, but primarily they acted as scouts and attrition units.","LocalizedString":"At the start of WWII the Imperial Japanese Navy had one of the world's most powerful submarine fleet. It was a varied fleet, from manned torpedoes to the Sentoku I-400-Class, which was the largest submarine of WWII. The fleet also included a number of fleet submarines, which many could carry an aircraft, and the Sentaka I-200-Class that reached the highest submerged speed of WWII. Despite having an advanced submarine fleet they were built in relatively small numbers and they were less effective than German submarines. The reason was the Japanese naval doctrine which focused on large and decisive fleet battles, and consequently the submarines were used against warships rather than merchant ships, but primarily they acted as scouts and attrition units."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnEndOfTurn","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnStartofTurn"],"draftBaseWeight":0.7,"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_3.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_otsuga.t_otsuga","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/ELUSIVE_FORCE.ELUSIVE_FORCE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":341.0},"historyPhotoSource":"IJN Photobook Submarine / Submar